<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sasol</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1950–</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sasol is a South African chemicals and energy company founded by the state in 1950 to make fuel from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a>, using the Fischer–Tropsch process at Sasolburg and later at Secunda. Its synthetic fuels reduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s dependence on imported oil during the apartheid-era <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanctions">sanctions</a>. Privatised from 1979, it remains one of the country's largest companies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sasol.jpg" alt="Sasol" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tom Corser · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sasol_Corporate_Office_Johannesburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
